{"author":{"id":"7be502fc1252faa17034e20337c97f83224cb75681f6f2358da33e4e8d7e55b6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794789536,"nonce":"PYGflNXpeP83Ne3krYSkeRK6wys=","title":"Feature request: built-in, configurable HTTP to HTTPS redirect on the main listener","message":"Hello Zentinel team,\n\nthank you for Zentinel. We would like to request a built-in, configurable HTTP to HTTPS redirect on the main listener, so that no extra route or namespace is needed for it.\n\nCurrent state (tag 26.11_2, commit ea8ccf0):\n\n- ListenerConfig (crates/config/src/server.rs:76) has no redirect option. Its fields include id, address, protocol, tls, default_route and namespace (server.rs:76-105), and a service field (server.rs:114).\n- The linter already recognises the case: an HTTP listener on port 80 without TLS should use an HTTPS redirect (crates/config/src/validate/lint.rs:68-71). There is no setting that acts on this warning.\n- The example \"redirect-https\" (crates/proxy/docs/examples.md:41-82) sets only a Location header and no status code, so it does not redirect.\n- The redirect filter can do the job, but it has to be wired as a separate route in a namespace bound to the port-80 listener. The RedirectFilter documents 301 or 302 today (crates/config/src/filters.rs:1185). Its Location is built from scheme, host, port and path only (crates/proxy/src/proxy/filters.rs:241).\n\nWe tested this workaround pattern (a namespace listener plus a redirect filter) in 26.11_2. It works: the answer is a 301 with a Location header. The query string is not carried over to the Location.\n\nRequest: a listener-level option, for example `redirect-to-https #true` on a `protocol \"http\"` listener (naming is open). It would\n- answer with a configurable 301 or 308 to the same host and path (308 would be an addition to the 301 and 302 documented today),\n- preserve the query string,\n- guarantee that ACME HTTP-01 challenge requests keep precedence and are answered before the redirect, as documented for early_request_filter (crates/proxy/docs/acme.md:273-275).\n\nWould the maintainers be open to this? We are glad to test a pre-release.\n\nThank you.","files":null}]}